          <caption>
            <p>Types of Spina Bifida. Meningocele is a type of neural tube defect where the meninges, the protective membranes surrounding the spinal cord, protrude through a spinal defect, forming a sac filled with cerebrospinal fluid. Meningoceles are typically covered by skin and generally present without neurological symptoms. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?search=types+of+spina+bifida&#x00026;title=Special:MediaSearch&#x00026;go=Go&#x00026;type=image">Public Domain</ext-link>, via Wikimedia Commons</p>
